-- title:
--   Coefficient certificates (3/3) for Klein's form T under U
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s\in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta=-s$, $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, $2\beta^{2}=s-5$ and $s^{2}=5$. The assertion is a conjunction of ten polynomial identities, each an explicit integer-coefficient expression in $\alpha$ and $\beta$ alone (the element $s$ occurs only in the hypotheses), every one of them homogeneous of total degree $30$ in $\alpha,\beta$ and with the monomials restricted to those appearing in the displayed sums. Eight of the ten identities assert that the corresponding expression vanishes, namely the first, second, third, fourth, sixth, seventh, eighth and ninth; the fifth asserts that its expression equals $15930175781250$, and the tenth that $\beta^{30}+522\,\alpha^{5}\beta^{25}-10005\,\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}-10005\,\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}-522\,\alpha^{25}\beta^{5}+\alpha^{30}=30517578125$. Each conjunct is thus a finite algebraic consequence, over any such $K$, of the four stated relations.
--
--   With $\zeta$ a primitive fifth root of unity and $\alpha=\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\beta=\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$, $s=\sqrt5$, these are the coefficient identities (the third and last block, for the higher powers of one variable) expressing the covariance of Klein's binary edge form $T$ of degree $30$ under the half-turn substitution generating the binary icosahedral group. It feeds [`RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU), en route to the icosahedral symmetry of the Rubin–Silverberg datum used for the family of elliptic curves with constant mod-$5$ representation.
-- source:
